e balance feels a lot better and  playing with it I actually really liked  it you have to actually pay attention  like my natural tendency when I put on  the rift is to put it like a little a  little high on my forehead because then  it kind of slowly falls down into place  whereas this headset I actually found  myself kind of pulling it down to get  things to line up again so that's pretty  cool  so I'm so far I'm pretty happy this like  loosens and tightens and there's a  button here on the bottom that extends  or retracts this for glasses people so  mine's all the way out because I have  glasses it does not solve your problems  so I think over time these lenses will  still get scratched if you're wearing  glasses you can buy like prescription  lenses to put in there or you can I've  got a 3d printer now so I've actually  I'm actually just going to print some of  these and then I bought some lenses from  xeni if anybody is curious about that  you can ask in the description I found  somebody put something on Thingiverse  pretty cool anyways so yeah so that's  the headset now the controller so these  are the new controllers here really the  biggest change from the CV one is like  this little hoop thing is now at the top  of the controller which as a subtle  benefit that I'm not really sure this is  what they were going for but now when  you put the controllers down like you  can actually set them down whereas this  is one of the older this is the CV 1  controller there was like no good way to  put these down like you could sort of do  that but it still would like roll around  these just nice bang done I love it  they're also a little fatter so they  feel better in your hand  so I'm actually I think these are better  it's just when you have this over your  face I'm so used to finding the hoop and  then like slipping my hand through the  hoop I go it's just been become second  nature for me so with these it's like  the actual opposite and I find myself  getting very confused when I'm in VR  like trying to get these freaking on my  hands I keep trying to do this and I'm  like wait what's going on Oh anyway I  just have to learn the new the new grips  now but otherwise everything's pretty  much the same  in terms of like the buttons and all  that no big difference so now in  playtime I use my VR headsets for really  two major types of games I play a  driving simulator type game so it's like  I'm just in a cockpit or like elite  dangerous which again you're just it's  like a space fighting game and again  you're in a cockpit so you're really not  moving around that much and then the  other games that I play are like FPS  games like first-person shooter games  which is what really drove me to this  headset because the room scale stuff is  very difficult with these first-person  shooter games so I've got a sunroom that  I like to play in but setting that  sunroom up to be  I can't just dedicate that to a VR room  so having it with inside out tracking  what sounded like a really cool option  so I've done that I've played probably  maybe one to two hours in onward with  the new rift s and I would say it's  pretty darn good I don't really have too  many issues with that their only thing  that I've noticed is sometimes the the  for whatever reason like when you start  lining up the two controllers this one  will get occluded which is not too  surprising because the tracking is right  on the headset so if you're like lining  up your sights you might actually  occlude the the controller's now with  onward I mean this is a brand new  headset and the way that they're doing  the tracking with with your hands and  stuff is in a way that doesn't really  suit this it works and it actually works  way better than I thought it would  already but I know that they're working  on updates already to fix that now now  comes really the biggest issue I've had  with this headset and that is this top  camera I'm so I'm using this in my son  room and my son 